id:                     E386
trigger_tool:           conan|autotools|automake|make
phase:                  configure|testing
error_signature:        getcwd.*diagnostic|working directory.*invalid|Permission denied.*RunTest|LOG_COMPILER.*RunGrepTest|configure.*noexec

severity:               2
category:               hmdfs, autotools, conan, testing, noexec
match_keywords:         capability-tested shell, getcwd, CONFIG_SHELL, SHELL, conanbuild, LOG_COMPILER, RunTest, RunGrepTest, direct ELF, HMDFS, noexec
title:                  Capability-tested shell and selective Automake dispatcher on noexec source trees

root_cause:             A HarmonyOS/HMDFS source or build tree can reject direct
                        execution of generated configure helpers and suffixless
                        shell test drivers. A shell binary may still return zero
                        while emitting a getcwd diagnostic, so executable-bit or
                        return-code checks alone do not prove that it can preserve
                        the requested working directory. Automake test lists can
                        mix shell drivers with real ELF tests; routing every test
                        through a shell would change the test semantics. Conan
                        self.run may also source conanbuild after the recipe has
                        selected a shell, silently replacing the tested path.
affected_scope:         Conan Autotools recipes built from noexec or HMDFS-style
                        paths with mixed suffixless shell and direct ELF Automake
                        tests, especially native OpenHarmony builds.
verification_cmd:       Run a fresh target conan create with a child-process
                        `pwd` probe whose stdout and stderr are both empty; bind
                        CONFIG_SHELL and SHELL to that path; run `make -j1 check`
                        through a selective LOG_COMPILER dispatcher; require the
                        complete upstream inventory and a real consumer to pass.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:            capability-tested-shell-and-selective-dispatch
rec_description:        Probe each candidate shell from the real build directory
                        and accept it only when `pwd` returns zero with empty
                        output and diagnostics. Reassert the resulting shell in
                        an explicit environment script after Conan's conanbuild
                        environment is sourced. Set CONFIG_SHELL and SHELL for
                        Autoconf, and use LOG_COMPILER only for known suffixless
                        shell drivers; direct ELF tests must continue to exec
                        directly.
rec_command:            make -j1 check LOG_COMPILER='<tested-shell> -c <dispatcher>'
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-and-test-launcher

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      executable-backed-test-root
fallback_description:   Move the source/build tree to a filesystem with proven
                        script execution only when the project cannot express a
                        selective launcher; keep the upstream test inventory and
                        direct-ELF distinction unchanged.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       shell -c.*all.*TESTS|LOG_COMPILER=/system/bin/sh.*unconditional
forbid_1_reason:        Sending every Automake entry to a shell attempts to parse
                        real ELF tests as scripts and can hide a missing test.
forbid_1_consequence:   The upstream test result is no longer authoritative.
forbid_2_pattern:       chmod \+x.*all|accept.*pwd.*stderr|os\.environ.*CONFIG_SHELL
forbid_2_reason:        chmod does not establish HMDFS execution capability, a
                        noisy pwd probe can poison Autoconf, and Conan buildenv
                        values are not guaranteed in the recipe Python process.
forbid_2_consequence:   The recipe can pass a local probe but fail at configure
                        or silently use a different shell in later stages.

principles:             P005,P010,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E087,E228,E232]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

